cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Are Fairness Scores in Crime Prediction Telling Us the Truth?
message: If you use this code or these findings, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gaurav
    family-names: Jha
abstract: >-
  Reported fairness gaps in crime-prediction models are largely explained by
  base rates rather than model quality, and base-rate correction alone is
  insufficient because a model can close a corrected gap by shifting its
  decision threshold while its ranking ability degrades. Includes a
  physics-informed model using the Short et al. (2008) burglary hotspot
  equations.
keywords:
  - algorithmic fairness
  - crime prediction
  - evaluation metrics
  - predictive policing
  - physics-informed neural networks
license: MIT
